CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*address_of error.*not an lvalue$
^.*bad reference initializer$
--
Per [expr.reinterpret.cast]/11 and [expr.unary.op]/3:
reinterpret_cast<T&>(x) yields an lvalue to the same storage, and
taking &<reference> yields the address of the referred-to object.
The MSVC <atomic> _Atomic_lock_acquire pattern (`&reinterpret_cast<
int&>(_Spinlock)`) tripped both of these.
